        "comments": "URL -- http://www.jgi.doe.gov/thalassiosira\nJGI Project ID: 2662235\nContacts: E. Virginia Armbrust (armbrust@u.washington.edu)\nIgor Grigoriev (ivgrigoriev@lbl.gov)\nThe clone of P. pseudonana that was sequenced is CCMP1335 and is available from the Center for Culture of Marine Phytoplankton (http://ccmp.bigelow.org). This clone was collected in 1958 from Moriches Bay (Long Island, New York) and has been maintained continuously in culture.\nAnnotation was done by the JGI Annotation team and the Diatom Consortium.\nChromosomes 7 and 18 are complete and present in GenBank records CP001160 and CP001159, respectively.\nThe JGI and collaborators endorse the principles for the distribution and use of large scale sequencing data adopted by the larger genome sequencing community and urge users of this data to follow them. It is our intention to publish the work of this project in a timely fashion and we welcome collaborative interaction on the project and analysis.\n(http://www.genome.gov/page.cfm?pageID=10506376)\nAnnotated scaffolds were added in January 2009.",
